4\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-24f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{2}-2\\cdot 12f+{12}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=12.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f-12)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48f257af-1f00-5cf9-89cd-3d44d21482ec" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Trinomial with Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f1b3aa-ebc1-51c1-8273-c4b915d8ecf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{25}{16})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481826} {:answer/id #uuid "3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481928} {:answer/id #uuid "7e777da0-d7e0-58cc-ba96-49a1a74e9598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{16})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482064} {:answer/id #uuid "898c7c3f-dd8f-5773-abc2-e29cff260011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{25}{4})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482094} {:answer/id #uuid "9d033726-a4f4-50d9-b131-7a5467c7dc90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d534e72-0930-51b5-a1d0-f3aa1de73e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(n+\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481928} :answer-field/id #uuid "6650d077-6bfe-5e18-8868-b906e55313a6" :answer-field/key "selectio